body:
@colis : 
After some intense debugging session I found out that when reloading the page with the initial query, `removeWidgets` gets called on the `taxonomies.auction_tax.name` refinement list which makes InstantSearch cleanup the state thus resetting the query. So you have to make sure your `<RefinementList>` or `useRefinementList` is mounted once and not unmounted later.
It most likely doesn't have anything to do with Next.js or the router.
There's something important to know when using React InstantSearch Hooks, it's that unmounting a widget component or hook cleans up its state. Which means if you do conditional rendering you have to be very careful. There's a guide for you to know more about it : https://www.algolia.com/doc/guides/building-search-ui/widgets/show-and-hide-widgets/react-hooks/

